" ---- strings and characters -----------------------------------
syn region  curryString start=/"/ skip=/\\\\\|\\"/ end=/"/ contains=curryStringEscape
syn match   curryStringEscape /\\\%([abntr\\"]\|x\x\+;\?\)/ contained
syn match   curryChar /#\\\%(x\x\+\|alarm\|backspace\|delete\|escape\|newline\|null\|return\|space\|tab\|.\)/

" ---- booleans, keyword objects, quoting -----------------------
syn match   curryBoolean /#\%(true\|false\|t\|f\)\%([[:space:]()\[\]\x27`",;]\|$\)\@=/
syn match   curryKeywordObj /#:[^[:space:]()\[\]\x27`",;]\+/
syn match   curryQuote /['`]\|,@\?/

" ---- numbers ---------------------------------------------------
syn match   curryNumber /\%(^\|[[:space:]()\[\]\x27`",;]\)\@<=[-+]\?\d\+\%(\/\d\+\|\.\d*\%([eE][-+]\?\d\+\)\?\)\?\%([[:space:]()\[\]\x27`",;]\|$\)\@=/
syn match   curryRadixNumber /#[bodxBODX][-+]\?[0-9a-fA-F]\+\%(\/[0-9a-fA-F]\+\)\?/
" Neugebauer sexagesimal: #s1;30 = 3/2, #s1,0,0 = 3600
syn match   currySexagesimal /#[sS]\d\+\%(,\d\+\)*\%(;\d\+\%(,\d\+\)*\)\?/
" Cuneiform numerals 𒁹=1 𒌋=10 𒑊=0.  The reader merges single-space-
" separated glyph groups into ONE token, then checks the synonym table,
" then parses as a sexagesimal number.  So a lone group defers to a
" synonym (𒁹 is `define`, 𒁹𒁹𒁹 is `newline`) but a spaced multi-group
" run is always a number (𒁹 𒌋𒁹 = 71).  Vim priority is definition
" order (later wins at the same position): single-group number here,
" synonyms after it, multi-group number last.
syn match   curryCuneiformNumber /\%(^\|[[:space:]()\[\]\x27`",;]\)\@<=[𒁹𒌋𒑊]\+\%([[:space:]()\[\]\x27`",;]\|$\)\@=/

